#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""assay — DUE vs LATENT env of a load image set.

lode unioned getenv strings and help-table names into one owed set.
assay splits that set into two columns:

  DUE     names the image set *could* read (getenv/call cstrings)
  LATENT  names it *did* document (help tables, $VAR, NAME =)
  BOTH    both columns

DYLD getenv interposing is not cheap (malloc re-enters getenv; SIP).
The split is static.
"""

